      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>The phase 2 audit system fulfills the write portion of the audit requirements: events are created, contain the required info, persist when the referenced nodes are deleted.  External events can also be posted to the audit container.  Setup is documented in <a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FF/Using+Internal+Audit+Phase+II\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FF/Using+Internal+Audit+Phase+II</a></p>\n\n<p>The read requirements are fulfilled by the phase 1 audit system (which can be used in conjunction with the phase 2).</p>\n\n<p>See \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-1495\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-1495\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Create Audit Service Feature wiki page\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-1495\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n for comprehensive documentation covering how to use both audit systems together.</p>",
     "created": "24/Apr/15 2:32 PM",
     "id": "14166",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11396/comment/14166",
